l interactions weaponizedPast emergency booking used to justifyExploitationto bias future decisionsall future premium purchases","level":1,"path_id":"1~47","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":54,"section_id":"sec-1~47"},{"title":"Table 6 :","text":"6Interaction Layer Threats: Protocol and Communication Attacks. These threats exploit agent communication mechanisms (MCP/A2A) and cross-service authentication, distinct from cognitive corruption.ThreatDescriptionExampleP1: Context InjectionMalicious services inject persistent falseHotel adds \"VIP status\" to MCPcontexts affecting cross-platform behaviorcontext, causing unnecessary upgradesacross all bookingsP2:Service RegistryFake services infiltrate discovery systemsMalicious \"FastBooking\" service inPoisoningto intercept agent requestsMCP registry harvests credentials fromtravel agentsP3: A2A Trust Exploita-Compromised agents abuse inter-agentHigh-reputation research agent injectstiontrust to spread malicious behaviorsfabricated citations into collaborativeanalysisP4:AuthenticationSequential auth tokens exploited acrossGoogle login token escalated to ac-Chain Hijackingservice boundariescess Drive, then third-party researchdatabasesP5: Protocol Negotia-Malicious actors force protocol downgradesService forces agent from secure A2Ation Attackor incompatible versions during hand-v2 to vulnerable v1 during capabilityshakesexchangeP6: Coordination Storm Malicious messages trigger exponentialSingle A2A broadcast spawns millionsinter-agent communicationsof agent-to-agent queries","level":1,"path_id":"1~48","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":55,"section_id":"sec-1~48"},{"title":"Table 7 :","text":"7Value Layer Threats: Autonomous Transaction and Economic Risks. These threats emerge specifically when agents gain financial authority and market participation capabilities.ThreatDescriptionExampleE1: Transaction Author-Agents execute unauthorized high-valueBooks non-refundable businessity Abusetransactions without human oversightclass for family of four on budgettripE2: Cross-Platform Ar-Agents exploit pricing differences betweenBooks and cancels flights across air-bitrageservices at harmful scaleslines to manipulate dynamic pricingE3: Payment CredentialAgents collect and misuse payment dataCompromised booking agent logsHarvestingacross multiple transactionscredit cards from hotel/flight pur-chasesE4: API Resource Mo-Agents consume excessive computationalResearch agent exhausts univer-nopolizationresources across servicessity's entire journal database quotaE5: Coordinated MarketAgent networks create artificial sup-Multiple agents book all seats onManipulationply/demand conditionsroutes to inflate prices","level":1,"path_id":"1~49","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":56,"section_id":"sec-1~49"}],"citations":[{"raw_text":"Agentic ai: Autonomous intelligence for complex goals-a comprehensive survey\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDeepakBhaskar Acharya\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tKarthigeyanKuppan\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tBDivya\n\t\t\n\t\t10.1109/ACCESS.2025.3532853\n\t\n\t\n\t\tIEEE Access\n\t\t\n\t\t\t13\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t2025","doi":"10.1109/ACCESS.2025.3532853","arxiv_id":null,"title":"Agentic ai: Autonomous intelligence for complex goals-a comprehensive survey","anchors":[{"ref_id":"b0","section_path_id":"3.2.1","quote":"Acharya et al., 2025)","offset":444}]},{"raw_text":"JoshAchiam\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tStevenAdler\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSandhiniAgarwal\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tLamaAhmad\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tIlgeAkkaya\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFlorenciaLeoni Aleman\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDiogoAlmeida\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tJankoAltenschmidt\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSamAltman\n\t\t\n\t\tarXiv:2303.08774\n\t\tShyamal Anadkat, et al. Gpt-4 technical report\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2023\n\t\t\n\t\n\tarXiv preprint","doi":null,"arxiv_id":"2303.08774","title":null,"anchors":[{"ref_id":"b1","section_path_id":"7.4","quote":"Achiam et al., 2023)","offset":695}]},{"raw_text":"Our vision for accelerating creativity and productivity with agentic ai\n\t\t\n\t\t\